[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m So, let's break it down. Let me define some variables first.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m Let t be the time she spends in the coffee shop in minutes. So, in the first case, when she walks at speed s, the total time is 4 hours, which is 4 * 60 = 240 minutes. But this total time includes t minutes in the shop, so the actual walking time must be 240 - t minutes.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m Similarly, when she walks at s + 2 km/h, the total time is 2 hours and 24 minutes, which is 2 * 60 + 24 = 144 minutes. Again, this total time is 144 minutes, which includes t minutes in the shop, so the walking time is 144 - t minutes.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m We can set up equations for both situations.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m First scenario:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m Walking speed = s km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m Distance = 9 km
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m Total time (including coffee) = 240 minutes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m Walking time = 240 - t minutes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m So, the time taken to walk 9 km at speed s is (240 - t) minutes. But the formula for time is distance divided by speed. However, the speed is given in km/h, so let's convert walking time from minutes to hours. That is, (240 - t) minutes is (240 - t)/60 hours.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m So, the equation is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m 9 / s = (240 - t)/60
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m Similarly, for the second scenario, when speed is s + 2:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m Total time = 144 minutes, so walking time is 144 - t minutes.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m Convert walking time to hours: (144 - t)/60
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m So, the equation is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m 9 / (s + 2) = (144 - t)/60
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m So now we have two equations:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=113897)[0m 1) 9 / s = (240 - t)/60
